Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:31:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Check save state loads against in-game saves

The in-game menu's Quick save/Quick load and save state slots go through
XdSaveStates, the same as the three-finger gestures. A save state also
restores the memory card, so loading one made before an in-game save
would leave the player with two different saves. XdSaveStates only loads
a state while the memory card is unchanged since the state was made.

To tell, it compares the card files with what they held when the state
was made. Dolphin writes the card files a while after the game saves (1 s
for GCI folders, up to 15 s for raw cards). So the memory card device
also records when the game last wrote to a card, exposed as
NativeLibrary.GetLastMemoryCardWriteTime().
